{"tool_name":"torchmd","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"torchmd","home":"http://www.torchmd.org/","license":"MIT","summary":"TorchMD is a deep learning framework for molecular simulations.","addition_date":"2021-12-13T10:18:44.278629Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:14:22.532282Z","tool_type":["Workbench"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:torchmd","credit":[{"email":"g.defabritiis@gmail.com","name":"Gianni De Fabritiis","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3913-4877","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Forcefield parameterisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3893"},{"term":"Molecular dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2476"},{"term":"Network analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3927"},{"term":"Protein folding analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2415"}]}],"name":"TorchMD","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jctc.0c01343","metadata":{"abstract":"Molecular dynamics simulations provide a mechanistic description of molecules by relying on empirical potentials. The quality and transferability of such potentials can be improved leveraging data-driven models derived with machine learning approaches. Here, we present TorchMD, a framework for molecular simulations with mixed classical and machine learning potentials. All force computations including bond, angle, dihedral, Lennard-Jones, and Coulomb interactions are expressed as PyTorch arrays and operations. Moreover, TorchMD enables learning and simulating neural network potentials. We validate it using standard Amber all-atom simulations, learning an ab initio potential, performing an end-to-end training, and finally learning and simulating a coarse-grained model for protein folding. We believe that TorchMD provides a useful tool set to support molecular simulations of machine learning potentials. Code and data are freely available at github.com/torchmd.","authors":[{"name":"Clementi C."},{"name":"De Fabritiis G."},{"name":"Doerr S."},{"name":"Giorgino T."},{"name":"Kramer A."},{"name":"Majewski M."},{"name":"Noe F."},{"name":"Perez A."}],"citationCount":136,"date":"2021-04-13T00:00:00Z","journal":"Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation","title":"TorchMD: A Deep Learning Framework for Molecular Simulations"},"pmcid":"PMC8486166","pmid":"33729795","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Chemistry","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3314"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Molecular dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0176"},{"term":"Protein folds and structural domains","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0736"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"TorchMD","home":"https://bio.tools/torchmd","license":"MIT","summary":"TorchMD is a deep learning framework for molecular simulations.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:torchmd/workbench/www.torchmd.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true,"repository":{}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":70,"citations":[{"count":4,"year":"2021"},{"count":7,"year":"2022"},{"count":8,"year":"2026"},{"count":11,"year":"2024"},{"count":19,"year":"2023"},{"count":21,"year":"2025"}],"doi":"10.1021/acs.jctc.0c01343","pmcid":"PMC8486166","pmid":"33729795","ref_count":41,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1999"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2005"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":1,"year":"2012"},{"count":1,"year":"2015"},{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":2,"year":"2009"},{"count":2,"year":"2011"},{"count":2,"year":"2014"},{"count":2,"year":"2016"},{"coun